### ST funding/quality/sale/body
89:**ST6 — FUNDING IS A DERIVED BAND, NEVER A COIN STORE; THE DM'S BAND IS A CEILING.** [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — the brief's "the ONE upkeep-shaped sink (the `UPKEEP_LEDGERS` row the champions volume uses)" does not exist: `UPKEEP_LEDGERS = ['deployments']`, `advanceTreasury(settlement, options = {})` takes no worldState and is called once from the frozen kernel.] A holder's DERIVED band is read each tick from what it has: a settlement from its prosperity label (`settlementFundingBand`, §2.4 — THE ONE settlement band, which THE PATROLS' pay gate reads too), a creed from its standing in the holder's seat town, a person from its purse band (CH's derived purse), a BODY (a gang, or a conclave holding as `faith`) from its own supplies and never above `meagre` — THE REPAIR CEILING, lifted for a conclave only by a patron court that endows its creed (§2.4; L-BD 31) — and a menace or a beast from nothing (its sites only wear) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 31]. The DM may set a band by hand (`fundingSet`), and it is a CEILING: the EFFECTIVE band is `min(fundingSet, derived)` on the order `unfunded < meagre < funded < lavish`, so a holder whose prosperity falls lets its sites go even under a DM's band — the owner's "these areas can also simply be abandonded due to lower prosperity" fires on every world now, before any treasury lights — and the DM's band can only hold a site LOWER than the holder's means (a lord who stops paying). THE DM'S LEVERS ON A POOR HOLDER'S KEEP ARE TWO, both through the record and neither a site override: the HOLDER — `SITE_HOLDER` hands the keep to a holder whose means pay for it (a richer court, a crown, a creed's seat) — and the HOLDER'S OWN MEANS, which are the settlement's prosperity and move only where the settlement's own economy moves (the landed upswing mover steps it, `upswingKernel.js`: "`economicState: { ...ec, prosperity: nextProsperity }`"; a DM act on the settlement where one exists — PLAUSIBLE, no landed edit of `economicState.prosperity` was found at master, `cure/D-ST-r3.md` Q1). Re-garrisoning a keep with a holder that is still `unfunded` buys it ONE season, never more: every holder change drops the want's clock (`wantSince`, §6.1 step 3) and the clock re-arms on the next unfunded read, so the new garrison walks away a season later, in the open, with its receipt; and EVERY HOLDER CHANGE DROPS THE DM'S CEILING (`fundingSet`) WITH THE CLOCK — the holder compared as its FULL IDENTITY (class · ref · role · creed, §2.1) — so a new holder starts from its own derived band and the DM's first lever works the tick it is pulled (a keep a lord stopped paying for, handed to `Prosperous` Ashford, is `lavish` at once; S3b) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.20 · ST-r2-16 (a)(b): the r3 cure compared `holder.ref` alone, so Kell's garrison → Kell's clergy kept the stale clock, and never dropped `fundingSet`, so the "lord who stops paying" ceiling (`unfunded`) outlived the lord and the new holder abandoned a season later]. A BODY holder's want is its own supplies: it keeps or leaves a site by its own weekly choice (THE BODIES §4, through ST's writer), never by this clock (§6.1 step 3). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-r2-16 (RULINGS-ROUND3 B): round 2's "to keep a poor town's keep manned regardless, the DM re-garrisons it by `SITE_HOLDER`" was false — the stale clock abandoned it again at once, and even a fresh clock cannot lift `min(fundingSet, derived)` above the holder's means; "manned regardless" is STRUCK]. COIN is the W-COIN slot (RULINGS-ROUND2 D): ONE upkeep law (`treasury.js :: computeUpkeep`, "ONE LAW PARAMETERIZED BY LEDGER"), widened by `UPKEEP_LEDGERS` members each with its caller in the same act — W-SEAT SEAT-8's `civilContests` · `interventions` (their charters) and FP's `sites` · `retainers` (CH) · `patrols` (PR): one roster, one law. FP's three ride ONE leaf-first car, because the frozen kernel's only call passes no worldState ("`advanceTreasury(sieged, { interval: tickInterval, tick: worldState.tick, deployment, blockade, rules: simulationRules })`"): the holder's roll is carried on the settlement record `advanceTreasury` already receives, written by the owning stage through its `settlementUpdates` and read the next tick (CH OD-CH-10's car; PLAUSIBLE, measured at that unit) — never a leaf inside `treasury.js` reading worldState, never a kernel line. When it lands, the derived band reads the PAID share. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-1 (RULINGS-ROUND2b: the DM's band a ceiling over the prosperity-derived band; the rows the W-COIN slot with a named car) · SEAMS-r2-12 (COIN separated from the BAND; the settlement-keyed band exported for the owner's patrol word "also size and number of patrols gated by tier, population, and prosperity and internal secruity").]
