146:[CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-16 (`wantSince`) · HOST-r2-8 (`mapSiteRef`, `from`) · HOST-r2-19 (`keptSecret` replaces the compile's `hidden`, whose word was the map's PARTY secrecy state) · ST-r2-1 (`fundingSet` a ceiling): each round-2 field drop-when-absent, declared under OD-ST-1's taking (OD-ST-34).] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-r2-16 (RULINGS-ROUND3 B: `wantSince` RESETS on every holder change — the writer compares `holder.ref` before and after each event and drops the clock whenever it differs: `placed · garrisoned · taken · reclaimed · conveyed · ceded · granted · seized · consecrated · sold · cleared · abandoned`) · ST-V1 (`holder.seenBy?`, the at-hand witnesses of an untied arrival, written once at the arrival and dropped with the holder): declared under OD-ST-1's taking (OD-ST-40).] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.20 · ST-r2-16 (a)(b): the holder comparison is the FULL IDENTITY `{ class, ref.kind, ref.bodyKind, ref.id, role, creed }` (A.20's tuple `{ kind, id, role }` read as the class and the ref's kind both, plus the creed — Kell's garrison handed to Kell's own clergy, or one creed's clergy to another's at the same seat, IS a holder change) [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — `creed` and `ref.bodyKind` added to A.20's tuple, so no holder change the ruling names can slip past it], and `fundingSet` is DROPPED at every holder change (a new holder starts from its own derived band) · A.17 · ST-W2: `seenBy` entries carry the might band seen at their tick (`{ id, mightBand, tick }`), never a live read · A.3: `holder.might` only on an id-less authored gang: declared under OD-ST-1's taking (OD-ST-43).]
148:- **Holder.** `class ∈ HOLDER_CLASSES = settlement · faith · person · untied`. `ref` is the ONE actor-ref convention `{ kind, id? }` (fold §3.3.12): `settlement` → `{ kind: 'settlement', id }` with `role ∈ garrison · civil`; `faith` → the clergy of a creed, `creed` the deity key, served EITHER by a SEAT — `{ kind: 'settlement', id: <the seat whose clergy serve> }` — OR by a CONCLAVE, THE BODIES' moving flock — `{ kind: 'body', bodyKind: 'conclave', id }` (a conclave's site is a church's, never a hazard: BD §2.1); `person` → `{ kind: 'person', id: 'wnpc_…' }` (a ledger person; a paragon's living `polarity` decides its sign, §3.1); `untied` → `{ kind: 'menace', id }` (MN's record — its might is READ through MN, never copied) or `{ kind: 'body', bodyKind: 'gang' | 'beast', id }` (THE BODIES' record, `spatialLedgers.bodies` — its might is READ from it, never copied; a lair is a site held by a beast, no new kind). BEFORE THE BODIES LAND (C15 precedes C17) a DM-AUTHORED gang is `{ kind: 'body', bodyKind: 'gang' }` with NO `id` and the DM's `might` on `holder.might` — the ONLY holder whose might ST stores — and BD-0's adoption (BD §3.2 (b) `den_held`) mints its body record, fills the `id` and drops `holder.might` through ST's one writer, so from then the record's might is the one truth. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.3 · SEAMS-r3-1 (BLOCKING) · ST-W1 · BD's route (1) and (4): the compile's `{ kind: 'band', id? }` and `{ kind: 'cult', id? }` are STRUCK as holder kinds — `band` is the landed SIZE word (708 src files; four of this volume's own vocabularies are "bands") and `cult` is the faith ladder's landed STANDING (`religionState.js :: standingFor`: "`… (share >= E ? 'established' : 'cult')`"), and the owner's "remember that not all cults are evil. cults are simply small conclaves of religion" (BOARD ~17:27) forbids a cult read as a hazard; in this volume `cult` now means the faith standing only (§2.4) — `D-ST-r4-probe/census-r4.out`.] THE ACTOR CONVENTION IS THE SIX KINDS `settlement · person · party · menace · corps · body` (A.12; RULINGS-ROUND3 §G.3, `bodyKind` a field): a body DECIDES (its weekly choice is its own, BD §4), so on a hearing card a body holder or arriver is an actor `{ kind: 'body', id }`; the convention gains no `site` (a WHERE and a subject, never an actor — it has no mind, ST4); an id-less authored gang has no record and no mind of its own, so it rides the `subject` dial as its holder ref until BD-0 adopts it. [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — `band` and `cult` holder REF kinds — ↳ r4: WITHDRAWN by A.3.] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-r2-14 (the RULINGS-ROUND2b ADDENDUM, applied; A.7): the compile's "the convention widens by `site` alone" is WITHDRAWN; `site` is a WHERE and a subject, never an actor — ↳ r4: A.7's five kinds amended to six by A.12; "a band or a cult … until WC-12 mints a band actor" superseded by THE BODIES' `body` actor.]
