174:| `FUNDING_BANDS` | `unfunded · meagre · funded · lavish` | what the holder can spend on it — the EFFECTIVE band `min(fundingSet, derived)` (ST6). [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — the brief's `none · thin · fair · full`: `thin` is MN's might word on the same cards (`thin · modest · capable · strong · formidable`), `fair` 12 and `full` 30 string-literal files on master; `meagre` and `lavish` are free, `unfunded` free as a literal] |
175:| `SITE_READINESS` | `at_strength · manned · sparse · skeleton · hollow` | a HELD site's garrison word — what H13's `PolitySite` reports as the "garrison band" and the dossier's site line shows — read from the site's ONE value `siteReadiness01` (§2.4): ≥ 0.75 `at_strength` · ≥ 0.40 `manned` · ≥ 0.20 `sparse` · > 0 `skeleton` · 0 `hollow` (DRAFT thresholds, UNMEASURED; `cure/D-ST-r3-probe/readiness.out` tables all twelve funding × quality cells — a lavish or funded sound keep is `at_strength`, a meagre sound one `manned`, an unfunded one `skeleton`, a ruined one `hollow`). It shares NO word with `STRENGTH_BANDS` (`thin · modest · capable · strong · formidable` — the army's and MN's might scale, which a homonym on the same card would make lie). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-V3 (A.10).] [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — the chair's proposed set was `full · manned · sparse · skeleton · empty`; by census two collide: `full` (37 quoted src files — infoMode `full`, a chain status, `politicalAutonomy` — the same reason round 1 refused it for `FUNDING_BANDS`, row below) and `empty` (16 quoted src files, AND this volume's own word for an UNHELD site on the same card — "The keep at Thornwatch has stood empty", ST7, §14 line 4); taken instead: `at_strength` (FREE, 0 everywhere) and `hollow` (0 quoted; prose only). `manned` 0 quoted; `sparse` 1 quoted (`settlement.schema.js` `proseDensity` — generation config, another surface; registered); `skeleton` 0 quoted (UI loader component names; registered) — `cure/D-ST-r3-probe/census-r3.out`, `census-r3b.out`. The fold §5's registration follows these five (routed).] |
184:- `settlementFundingBand(worldState, settlementId, snapshot) → FUNDING_BAND` — THE ONE settlement band: its `prosperityRank01` (`< 0.2` unfunded · `< 0.45` meagre · `< 0.8` funded · else lavish, DRAFT), exported for THE PATROLS' pay gate (PR §3.1) and CH's retainers [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-12: PR needs a settlement-keyed band; the site read was keyed by site] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — note 2 · PR-V6 (A.9): ONE name, this one; PR's `fundingBandOfSettlement` is renamed in PR (routed)].
185:- `fundingBandOf(worldState, siteId, snapshot) → FUNDING_BAND` — the EFFECTIVE band `min(fundingSet, derived)` [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-1]; derived by holder: a settlement by `settlementFundingBand`; a SEAT's clergy by its creed's standing band in that seat town (`cult` unfunded · `established` funded · `ascendant` lavish — the faith contest's landed standing words, PLAUSIBLE until ST-3's car-0 names the field); a person by CH's derived purse band (a slot until CH lights; `meagre` meanwhile); a menace and an id-less authored gang `unfunded`; a BODY holder (gang or conclave) by its OWN supply stock — THE REPAIR CEILING (L-BD 31: "they lack the logistics"): `BODY_FUNDING_BY_SUPPLY` maps THE BODIES' supply word (`bodyReadiness01`'s `BODY_SUPPLY_WORDS`, BD §2.5) `provisioned` → `meagre` · `strained` → `unfunded` · `starving` → `unfunded`, so a body's band is NEVER above `meagre` — EXCEPT a conclave whose creed an attached court holds `endowed` (THE BODIES' `courtStanceOf`; RULINGS-ROUND3 §G.2: the one thing patronage buys), which repairs with that court's logistics: its band is the HIGHEST `settlementFundingBand` among the endowing courts attached to the site (codepoint tie-break) — THE PATRON'S LIFT; a BEAST is `unfunded` always and never repairs (L-BD 31: "Beasts never repair it"); with THE BODIES dark, every body holder reads `unfunded` (its sites only wear) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 31 · BD's route: the body holder's band, its ceiling and the patron's lift; `D-ST-r4-probe/census-r4.out` (`BODY_FUNDING_BY_SUPPLY` FREE); the readiness each band gives, `D-ST-r4-probe/arith.out`]. The DM's `fundingSet` is a ceiling over every one of these (ST6).
188:- `denPressOf(worldState, siteId, settlementId) → number` — how hard the site's holder presses ONE attached town: ST's own feeder term for that site at that town, or, where the handoff above gives a body's presence to THE BODIES, that body's own term in BD's row at that town (the per-body part of `bodyPresenceFeeder`, `PRESENCE_BY_MIGHT[might] × ACT_FACTOR[act]`, BD §8.2 — ROUTE BD: expose the per-body part by name) — so the clearing fork and the den's occasion (§6.1 step 6, §6.6) read the ONE term the composer carries, never a second computation of it [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — the handoff would otherwise blind step 6 and §6.6, whose test "the ST presence feeder on that town ≥ 0.40" reads zero for every body's den once THE BODIES' effects light].
190:- `siteReadinessOf(worldState, siteId, snapshot) → { siteReadiness01, word }` — THE ONE READINESS VALUE of a held site (A.10): `siteReadiness01 = F(fundingBandOf) × Q(quality)` (§3.2's factors; × ½ for a `person` or `faith` holder of a `fortification`, §3.2), and its word on `SITE_READINESS` (§2.3); an unheld site has none (ST7). For an UNTIED holder the value is the WALLS manned at that holder's means (a menace `unfunded`; a body by its supply word, never above `meagre` — the repair ceiling) and enters the site's own siege and clearing contests (§8); its card word stays the holder's might, never a garrison word (below) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (3) · L-BD 31]. Every reader of a garrison reads THIS: the town's keep term, the site's own siege, the map's word [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-V3 (A.10): one value, one scale, one word]. [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — the value is minted `siteReadiness01`, not the ruling's `readiness01`: `readiness01` is LANDED as a town's and an army's MARTIAL readiness (14 src files; `WarTab.jsx :: readinessWords` prints "on a war footing" from it), and ST9 reads that index beside this one — two meanings of one token in one volume would be the homonym A.10 forbids (`cure/D-ST-r3-probe/census-r3.out`).]
193:- `believedDenOf(worldState, courtId, siteId, snapshot) → { known, holderRef?, mightBand?, sinceTick?, source? }` — what a COURT believes of a site held by a FORCE it may contest: an untied holder (a gang, a beast, a menace, an id-less authored gang) or a conclave the court holds `outlawed` (§6.1 step 6). ONE BELIEF OF A HOLDER'S MIGHT (A.17): it reads the holder's ONE belief read — a MENACE holder through MN's `believedMenaces(worldState, courtId)` (its `believedMight`, where the menace's newest entry places it at this site), a BODY holder through THE BODIES' `believedBodyOf(worldState, courtId, bodyId)` (L-BD 45's believed size band · den · last heard; BD's read), and only an id-less authored gang, which has no belief store of its own, through ST's own sighting rows — never a live truth read and never a second belief. THE SIGHTING (`source: 'seen'`): the one writer, at every event that installs a body or menace holder at a site that is NOT `keptSecret` (an arrival's `taken`, an authored placement, a `site_siege` fall, a body's own take, `made_known` of a held site), WRITES one entry `{ id, mightBand, tick }` into `holder.seenBy` for each court attached `at_hand` (the anchor; both ends of a road) — the might band SEEN at that tick, refreshed only when a court sees the holder again AT THE SITE at a dated act — a contest it fights there (`site_taken`'s sortie, `site_cleared`, `site_siege`) or a PATROL'S LOOK (THE PATROLS §9.2 (b): "A FINDING IS A SIGHTING … through ST's one writer as the site's `seenBy` entry with the might BAND seen then" — PR's one sighting input on ST's closed caller list, which writes or refreshes the looking court's row, whatever its distance band); THE ROW IS A REGISTERED SOURCE of the holder's one belief read — the `siteWitnesses` → `witnessedCrossing` idiom (ST17): MN's `believedMenaces` and BD's `believedBodyOf` compose it beside their tellings, newest by tick (ROUTE MN · BD), so a court that saw a `capable` host at the keep and later heard it called `strong` believes the newer — one read, never two pictures; a witness AWAY from the site (a raid on the court's land, the warden's office knowledge, L-BD 41) writes into that same one belief by its owner's door, never into ST's row. So the at-hand courts know the holder in the arrival's OWN week, in every preset — and the sighting is a written row, not a telling, for a MEASURED reason: the rumor stage seeds a tick's news BEFORE the calamity stage runs (`pulseKernel.js`: "`const rumors = advanceRumorLedgers({`" at ~2097, "`const calamity = advanceCalamity({`" at ~2527; `D-ST-r4-probe/measure-3.out`), so a telling written at the act reaches even its hop-0 holders a tick late [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.17's "a telling on its channel" kept as the holder's ONE belief read, with ST's row as a registered source of it, because a telling cannot be same-week (measured)]. THE TOLD ARM (`source: 'told'`): every other court — in the omniscient arm the truth from the tick after the act; in the belief presets the newest TELLING of the site it holds, whichever made or unmade the holder — `site_taken` (whose one writer is ST's, for the hearing's verdict AND an authored placement, cause `dm`), a `site_siege` fall, MN17's menace rumors for a menace holder, THE BODIES' rumor slots (`bodyId` · `bodyKind`, BD §2.4) for a body holder (the arrival's `site_taken` row carries MN17's typed `menaceId`/`menaceName` or BD's `bodyId`/`bodyKind`, so the told arm feeds the same one belief read), and against them the UNMAKING telling — ONE `site_cleared` news row, its word `cleared · driven_off · abandoned · ended` in the content, emitted by the one writer at EVERY event that ends a force's hold (a clearing, a menace's end, a body's end or departure, PT's `party_cleared_site`, the DM's `SITE_HOLDER` to none) — the anchor as the involved settlement, so the at-hand courts hold the unmaking telling as its hop-0 holders from the next tick (read-last, write-next); the might through MN17's might↔magnitude map or BD's slots; unheard ⇒ not known. THE VEIL (A.16): a `keptSecret` site emits NO telling — no arrival row, no authored-placement row, no `site_siege` fall, no unmaking row — and writes no sighting, until `made_known` (the DM's `SITE_STATUS`; the one writer then emits the telling of its current holder, cause `dm`, and writes the at-hand courts' sighting); until then a court learns of a kept-secret den ONLY by WITNESS — a patrol's look (PR), the warden (L-BD 41), the holder's own act seen on that court's land — written into the holder's one belief for THAT court alone, never a telling; in the omniscient arm a kept-secret site is known to no court [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.17 · ST-W2 (MAJOR): round 3's "a court in `seenBy` knows the holder, its might as it stands" read the menace's might live every tick (ST §2.1: "`might` is READ from it, never copied") while MN's relief read `believedMenaces` — two beliefs of one might; now the band seen at the tick, and ONE read per holder kind · A.16 · ST-W3 (MAJOR): the told arm had no `keptSecret` guard — the arrival and the authored row fired for a kept-secret shrine, so far courts were told while the at-hand court was blind · note 2: every unmaking event now emits its telling] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-15] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-V1 (RULINGS-ROUND3 B: no court could believe an arrival in its own week, so the folded contest could never fire — now the at-hand courts see it; the folded contest stands for them alone, §8) · ST-V2 (RULINGS-ROUND3 B: an authored den and a siege-taken keep made no telling, so every belief preset left them unanswerable — now every telling that makes an untied holder is read, and an authored placement EMITS the same `site_taken` row, one writer one kind)].
