230:| `faith` held by a CONCLAVE (THE BODIES' flock, ref `{ kind: 'body', bodyKind: 'conclave', id }`) | `tied` — BENEFITS, PER TOWN BY THAT TOWN'S STANCE TOWARD THE CREED | each attached town by distance band WHERE its court's stance toward the creed (THE BODIES' one read `courtStanceOf(worldState, snapshot, settlementId, 'creed:<ref>')`, whose default is the owner's alignment word — the patron's and the flock's gods' `stanceOf` distance, BD §7.1) is `permitted` or `endowed`; a town that holds the creed `curbed` or `outlawed` takes NOTHING from it (neither benefit nor hazard — it shuts the flock out; whatever harm a HOSTILE flock does is its own acts through THE BODIES' rows, one term per thing, BD §8.2/§9.2); the faith arm (the holding creed's local strength, §3.3 shrine) reaches the permitting and endowing towns only — in a curbing or outlawing town THE BODIES' stance multiplier on that creed's strength (BD §7.4) is the one lean (one term per thing); with THE BODIES dark the stance read is absent and the flock's site reads as any faith holder of its creed |
238:- TIED term — an ADDITIVE term is `BASE[kind][seam] × S`, and a GATE ROW (a multiplier) scales its DEVIATION from one, `mult = 1 + (BASE − 1) × S`, where `S = F(funding) × Q(quality) × D(distance)` [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-7 (RULINGS-ROUND2b): the literal product on a multiplier flipped its sign — an unfunded keep's ×0.8 read ×0.12 and a capable den's ×1.3 read ×0.78; now ×0.97 and ×1.18 (`cure/D-ST-r2-probe/scaleAndLatch.out`), never a sign flip]; `F`: unfunded 0.15 ("walls without defenders") · meagre 0.45 · funded 0.8 · lavish 1.0; `Q`: sound 1 · worn 0.5 · ruined 0; `D`: at_hand 1 · nearby 0.5 · distant 0.2. A `person` or `faith` holder of a `fortification` counts at half (a lord-errant's hall is not a garrison).
332:2. **Wear and restoration** (on a YEAR crossing, keyed by year — the rite idiom; `seasonForTick(...).year`): a tied holder at `funded`/`lavish` → `restored` one band if below `sound`; `meagre` → holds; `unfunded` → `worn` one band; an unheld or untied site → `worn` one band every second year (DRAFT, UNMEASURED). A `ruin` never changes quality. THE REPAIR CEILING (L-BD 31: "there is a ceiling to how much conclaves and gangs can bolster or repair … for they lack the logistics. Beasts never repair it"): a BODY holder's band is its supply word's (never above `meagre`, §2.4), so it HOLDS what it took — a `provisioned` gang or conclave PATCHES a `ruined` site up to `worn` in that year and never higher (`BODY_REPAIR_CEILING` = `worn`, DRAFT, UNMEASURED — a body cannot make a keep sound), a `strained` or `starving` body's site wears as an unheld one (every second year), a BEAST never repairs (its lair only wears, every second year); a conclave under THE PATRON'S LIFT (an attached court holds its creed `endowed`, §2.4) repairs as a tied holder at the patron's band, up to `sound`; and the keep's readiness follows the band (a body's sound keep reads at most `manned`, `siteReadiness01` ≤ 0.45; a conclave's at most `sparse`, × ½ as a faith holder of a fortification) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 31 · RULINGS-ROUND4 B (ST): the brief's "propose `sound`, never `lavish`/`at_strength`'s top" measured against ST's bands — `sound` is the TOP of the three quality bands, so the ceiling sits on the FUNDING the body can give (≤ `meagre`) and on the REPAIR it can make (to `worn`), and `at_strength` (≥ 0.75) is out of a body's reach without a patron].
333:3. **Abandonment by want** (the owner's "abandonded due to lower prosperity"; ruling 11a): a tied holder whose EFFECTIVE band (ST6: the DM's band is a ceiling over the derived one) has read `unfunded` for one season (DRAFT 13 weeks = `INTERVAL_WEEKS.one_season`, UNMEASURED) → `abandoned`, holder cleared, `lastHolder` set. The dwell is DECLARED: this step sets `wantSince` the first tick the effective band reads `unfunded` and drops it the first tick it reads above (drop-when-absent; §11), so a keep garrisoned years ago and starved today abandons one season after the want began, never on the first unfunded read [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-16 · ST-r2-1: "A DM-set band never abandons" is STRUCK (RULINGS-ROUND2b)]. AND THE ONE WRITER DROPS `wantSince` AND `fundingSet` ON EVERY HOLDER CHANGE — `applySiteEvent` compares the holder's FULL IDENTITY `{ class, ref.kind, ref.bodyKind, ref.id, role, creed }` before and after each event and drops both whenever any part differs (`placed · garrisoned · taken · reclaimed · conveyed · ceded · granted · seized · consecrated · sold · cleared · abandoned`, and a body's own take or leaving) — so the want and the DM's ceiling are always the CURRENT holder's [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.20 · ST-r2-16 (a)(b): Kell's garrison handed to Kell's own clergy (`ref` unchanged, `class` and `role` changed) IS a holder change; the ceiling no longer outlives its holder]. A BODY holder (gang or conclave) is EXEMPT from this step: its want is its supplies and its leaving is its own choice (THE BODIES §4; BD9: "Moving the base is a choice, never a drift"), so the step sets no `wantSince` for it [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — a conclave is a TIED `faith` holder, and the want clock would have walked a `strained` flock out of its shrine a season later by drift, against BD9]: a keep abandoned and re-garrisoned by the DM (`SITE_HOLDER`) starts a fresh clock, and a new holder that is still `unfunded` holds it one season, then walks away in the open (ST6 names the DM's real levers) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-r2-16 (RULINGS-ROUND3 B): round 2 dropped the clock only "when it reads above", which an `abandoned` holder never does, so the unheld site kept a stale `wantSince` and the DM's re-garrison was abandoned again on the next tick].
336:6. **Clearings:** an attached tied court whose town the den presses (`denPressOf` on that town ≥ 0.40, DRAFT — the one presence term the composer carries for that holder, ST's or THE BODIES', §2.4; a fact of its own land, felt on its own roads), which holds the den's holder HOSTILE (as step 4 defines it — so a conclave's site is cleared only by a court that holds its creed `outlawed`: the SEIZURE of L-BD 30, "the court's choice", which THE BODIES' stance makes hostile) and which BELIEVES it can contest the den (`believedDenOf`, §2.4: its FIELD FORCE `homeDefense − siteDefense` from the capacity lookup — the ready keep stays at its walls, A.1 · A.5 — against the den's defender AS IT BELIEVES IT, the holder's might seen or heard plus the site's walls (§8), ratio ≥ 1.2, DRAFT; truth only in the omniscient arm; a `keptSecret` den the court has not witnessed, or an unheard one, is never answered) SORTIES through its own `clearingFork` — the court's landed risk posture (`strategicPosture.js`, requirement 10) as the one bounded signal — → `site_cleared` at that week's climax, for a den ALREADY held before this week (an arrival this week is `site_taken`'s contest) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-15 · ST-r2-17] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.5 · A.18 · BD's route (2), (3): the sortie's force is the field force (round 3 read `offensive`, which counts an army marched elsewhere); the press reads the one term the composer carries]. ONE CONTEST PER SITE PER WEEK (A.18): the ANCHOR court leads when it sorties; every other court that sorties on the same den that week JOINS it as ONE force (field forces summed; each joiner receipted); when the anchor does not sortie, the sortieing court nearest by band leads (codepoint tie-break); never two contests. A reclaim's `moves` against an untied holder mints `site_cleared` at the NEXT week's climax (the docket resolves the reclaim first, and nothing it decides opens a second hearing in its own week — requirement 24(b)); a grouped patrol (THE PATROLS) is its court's sortie and joins that week's one contest at its band; a BODY may clear another body's site (BD §9.4); the party clears through PT's ONE door (§7.2) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-17 · ST-r2-19].
337:6b. **The forced sale** (L-BD 30: a non-hostile conclave "may not be pursued by settlement but may be forced to give it up in exchange for resources"): an attached court at `at_hand` that holds the site's conclave's creed `permitted` or `curbed` (never `endowed` — it keeps the flock; never `outlawed` — it clears, step 6), whose effective band is `funded` or better (it can pay), DEMANDS the site through its `saleFork` (no randomness) where the site is its own use — a `fortification` or `watchtower` at hand (its defence) or a site it last held (`lastHolder`) — at most once per court and site a year (DRAFT, UNMEASURED), and ONE demand per site per week (the anchor's first, A.18's rule) → `site_sale` at that week's climax (§8) [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — the producer's bounds (an at-hand court, `funded` or better, a site of its own use, once a year, one demand a week) are the lane's, so the sale never becomes a weekly lever on every flock]: the flock answers by its god's recorded axes, the price is paid in the flock's supplies, a refusal hardens the court's stance one step [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 30 · RULINGS-ROUND4 B (ST) — measured: ST's conveyance road is WR-10's court-to-court hearing ("Every holding a campaign court could convey"), whose conveyor must be a campaign court, so a body cannot sell through it; ST names its own kind `site_sale` (FREE, `D-ST-r4-probe/census-r4.out`), whose `sold` is already one of ST's own `SITE_EVENTS` and whose `refused` carries the conveyance row's own meaning — a holder declines to give up a holding].
365:| SOLD | between courts: the conveyance road with coin when the treasury lights (`treasuryEnabled`); dark meanwhile. BY A CONCLAVE to a court that demands it (L-BD 30's forced sale): ST's own `site_sale` hearing (§6.1 step 6b, §8) — the price paid in the flock's supplies through THE BODIES' one writer, the court's coin the W-COIN slot [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 30] | `sold` |
371:`site_reclaim` is offered to `lastHolder`'s court in the week the site falls empty or untied, BEFORE any other court's clearing or garrisoning may move on it that week. Its DEFAULT (the court's own fork, which draws no randomness): `reclaimScore = fundingRank (unfunded 0 · meagre 1 · funded 2 · lavish 3) + (against an untied holder) the believed force ratio's term (§6.1 step 6: ≥ 1.2 → +1, else −2) + the court's risk-posture term (requirement 10, ±1)`, and the court `moves` when it stands and `reclaimScore ≥ 1` (DRAFT, UNMEASURED); else `declines`. **The tilt** (requirement 24(b): "a declared bounded term on the decider's score where the decider draws no randomness"): ±1 slight · ±2 heavy on `reclaimScore` [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-18: every kind offers the three choices]. `moves` on an unheld site = `reclaimed` + `garrisoned`; on an untied one = the `site_cleared` contest at the NEXT week's climax (§6.1 step 6). A decline (or a court that cannot) opens the site to whoever acts next: the attached courts by distance band (nearest first, codepoint tie-break), the party by deed. A preference, never a right — nothing is forbidden, and the DM may decide any week.
379:THE OCCASION AND ITS TWO CLOSINGS (A.6) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.6 · SEAMS-r3-5 (MAJOR): round 3's occasion wrote `protection_failed` and nothing ever wrote `protection_kept` for a den the liege answered (ST: 0 hits), so the hold's `P` could only fall from it]. The occasion `den_unanswered` OPENS on a SWORN member's town the first week the den presses it at or above 0.40 (`denPressOf`, DRAFT) AND the liege could know it (the liege's `believedDenOf` holds the den; a liege is never blamed for a den it has not heard of) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-15], for a den the MEMBER holds hostile (§6.1 step 4's test — a den the member itself `tolerated`s, `employed`s or `harboured`s is the member's own choice, priced by PL's harbouring row where the liege hunts it, BD §7.1 → PL, never the liege's failure) and never for a `keptSecret` den (A.16 · OD-ST-35); its CLOCK is one season (DRAFT 13 weeks, UNMEASURED). It CLOSES ONCE, under its one episode `den_unanswered:<siteId>:<tick>` (`<tick>` the opening tick): `protection_kept` when the den is CLEARED within the clock — by the liege's answer (its own sortie if it is attached, its army through ST-2b, its riders, or a decided relief PL already owns) or by anyone (the member, a third court, a body, the party) — the member stood; `protection_failed` when the clock EXPIRES with the den still holding — the member was not protected, the receipt saying whether the liege came and was repelled ("Kell's lord came, but the robbers held the keep") or never came (A.1's principle: the outcome by harm, the answer on the receipt); and NO row when the den ends or leaves within the clock by its own course (a menace's end, a body's end or move — no protection was tested) [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.6 names the cleared and the unanswered closings; the repelled liege and the self-ending den are stated so every opened occasion closes exactly once]. ST supplies the occasion and PL records the outcome row on the sworn edge through its request door (`requestFealtyRow`, episode `den_unanswered:<siteId>:<tick>`, a registered `FEALTY_EPISODE_PREFIXES` member — PL §4) [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PL's request door (SEAMS-r2-10 is PL's) named for ST's occasion] — PL's one writer, the occasion registered in PL's own commit (the SEAMS-r1-2 registration idiom) — a row the crown's hold reads through its `P` (PL P43: "H's `P` falls by it" for `protection_failed`; its mirror rises by `protection_kept` — ROUTED to PL) and nothing else; BOTH closings ride the SAME flags (requested under `siteFatesEnabled` ∧ `polityEnabled`, A.5), so the den's two outcomes are symmetric under every legal flag set and never wait on `polityObligationsEnabled` (SEAMS-r3-5's one-way case closed on ST's side): the hold's `P` moves by OUTCOME and the request door patches trust only for `fealty_defied` (A.6), so the row carries no trust or resentment patch of its own; the occasion is requested under `siteFatesEnabled` ∧ `polityEnabled` (A.5: a requested row rides the requester's flag ∧ `polityEnabled`) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — A.5 · A.6: round 2's "carrying the member's resentment patch `protection_failed` already carries (PL §4.3, P9)" is narrowed to the truth A.6 rules]. So a crown that lets its border forts rot loses their protection AND makes dens that press its own members, and its hold frays by the protection record it already reads — and a crown whose riders clear the dens its members suffer is credited with the protection it gave, by the same record. The clock: weekly check from the opening, one season to close; the receipt names the den, the liege and the closing.
391:A CONCLAVE MAKES NO DEN (A.3): a flock that takes a site — by arrival at an empty one, or by clearing a hostile body's (L-BD 30) — holds it as `faith`, a church's site whose sign in each town follows that town's stance toward its creed (§3.1); a court that wants it back may DEMAND it against resources (`site_sale`, §6.1 step 6b) or, holding the creed `outlawed`, clear it (the seizure, step 6). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.3 · SEAMS-r3-1 (BLOCKING) · ST-W1: the rows "a cult | the faith system's own heresy" and "a DM-authored band or cult" STRUCK; the brigand row filled by THE BODIES (BD's route (1), (4)).]
430:The actor convention is SIX kinds, `settlement · person · party · menace · corps · body` (A.12, amending A.7 by RULINGS-ROUND3 §G.3 — the fold §1's requirement-24 bracket, the spine §1 mirror and the fold §3.3's row say six at P4): a corps decides (its weekly choice is its own; CH §16b) and is keyed `u:`; a menace stays an actor because the DM's authored course stands in for its mind (MN12 · MN6); a BODY decides (its weekly choice is its own, THE BODIES §4) and carries its kind as a field (`bodyKind ∈ conclave · gang · beast`, as a person's archetype is a field); A SITE HAS NO COURSE AND NO CHOICE (ST4: "A site has no mind"), so it is never an actor kind and `strategicPosture.js :: POSTURE_ACTOR_KINDS` — "THE CLOSED ACTOR SET" of posture-bearing deciders ("a posture read that quietly treats a temple as a settlement would be wrong in a way no gate could see") — gains no `site`. Both jobs a site has on a card are carried without it: the WHERE by `ENGAGEMENT_WHERE_KINDS`' `site` (the fold §3.4's companion table), the target by the `subject` dial (the proposals' `targetSaveId` stays the anchor settlement, MN9's convention). A BODY that holds, takes, besieges or clears a site is a PARTY of ST's hearings as the actor `{ kind: 'body', id }` (THE BODIES §9.4: "actor lists WIDENED"); only an id-less authored gang (before C17, §2.1), which has no record and no mind of its own, rides the `subject` dial as its holder ref until BD-0 adopts it. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.12 · BD's route (3): six kinds; a body an actor; "a band or a cult on a card rides the `subject` dial … until WC-12 mints a band actor" superseded by THE BODIES' `body`.] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-r2-14 (the RULINGS-ROUND2b ADDENDUM, "ACCEPTED as proposed", applied here and at ST18, §2.1, §7.4's SP row, §8's parties and OD-ST-27; L-ST item 20(b)'s "the actor convention gains `site`" is WITHDRAWN) · A.7 (the five kinds — ↳ r4: six, A.12) · FOLD-r2-verify's note ("ST still carries the STOP-era wording").]
436:| SP (the shared spine) | BY THE SITE READ — the WHERE `site` (`ENGAGEMENT_WHERE_KINDS`) and the `subject` dial; `POSTURE_ACTOR_KINDS` gains NO `site` (a site is never an actor — §7.3; the SIX actor kinds are A.12's, `body` the sixth) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — ST-r2-14 (the ADDENDUM, applied)] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.12]; SP-9's docket hosts ST's FIVE kinds (`registerEngagementKind`; `site_sale` the fifth, §8) |
456:| BD (the bodies) | BY BOTH — a body is a HOLDER (a gang or a beast `untied`; a conclave `faith`, §2.1) and an ACTOR of ST's hearings (§7.3, §8: it takes an empty site, besieges a held one, clears another body's); its den's presence and raider-gate rows are THE BODIES' own while `bodyEffectsEnabled` is lit (ST's read zero — one term per thing, §3.3), ST's on the record's might while dark; the holder body's `bodyStrength` stands on the defender's side beside the site's walls (§8); a body's band is its supply word, never above `meagre` — the repair ceiling — save a conclave a court endows (the patron's lift, §2.4, §6.1 step 2); a body's take, leaving and end go through ST's one writer (`arriveAt`, §6.1 steps 1 and 4); BD-0 ADOPTS every id-less authored gang into a body record by ST's writer (§2.1); a non-hostile flock's site may be bought (`site_sale`) and an outlawed one's cleared (§6.1 steps 6, 6b); the at-hand sightings are a registered source of THE BODIES' `believedBodyOf` (A.17) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (5): the coverage row] |
474:| `site_sale` | ST (ST-2) | `site` | the week an attached court DEMANDS a site a conclave holds, against resources (§6.1 step 6b; L-BD 30) | `sold · refused` | CLIMAX | the FLOCK's answer by its god's recorded axes, `saleFork` (no randomness): `saleScore = law + good`, `law` +1 lawful · 0 neutral · −1 chaotic, `good` +1 good · 0 neutral · −1 evil (`deityAxes.js :: chaos01` / `evil01` of the creed's deity: "lawful: 0", "good: 0"), `sold` when `saleScore ≥ 0` (DRAFT, UNMEASURED) — so a lawful flock yields at a fair price, a chaotic one may refuse, a good one yields (L-BD 30: "lawful yields at a fair price; chaotic may refuse; good yields where the people are served"); `sold` → the site passes to the court's garrison through ST's writer (`sold`; a holder change, §6.1 step 3) and THE PRICE is paid into the flock's supply stock by THE BODIES' one writer (DRAFT +0.5, capped at 1 — ROUTED to BD; the court's own coin is the W-COIN slot, a `sites` row, dark meanwhile — DRAFT, UNMEASURED, recorded); `refused` → the site stands and the refusal is an input of THE BODIES' `body_stance` fork for that court, one step toward `curbed` (L-BD 30's counterforce — ROUTED to BD); a SEIZURE is never this hearing's verdict: it is the court's own act once it holds the creed `outlawed` (`site_cleared`, §6.1 step 6) | the buyer `{ kind: 'settlement', id }` upon the flock `{ kind: 'body', id }`, the site as the card's WHERE | a bounded term on `saleScore`: ±1 slight · ±2 heavy — the decider draws no randomness (requirement 24(b)) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 30: ONE new kind, the fold's §3.4 count +1, WHERE `site` (ROUTED to the fold)] |
476:[REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — the brief's `site_fallen` (CLIMAX; `holds · falls`) and `site_siege` (STANDING; the siege words) were one fact heard twice; ONE kind, `site_siege`, carries it on the registry's one siege vocabulary.] **No party kind:** none of ST's kinds is a party kind; the party's dealings with a site are PT's doors, and requirement 24's party default ("nothing has happened to the party yet") is never ST's to compute. **Not hearings:** the party's reach (`party_reached_site`) and its hand on a site made known (`party_made_known_site`) — PT deed doors, never the engine deciding the party's fate [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — "the reveal" → PT's kind]; an authored force holder (the DM's act is the verdict; it is told, §6.2 — save at a kept-secret site, A.16); a body's own leaving or end (its course, receipted and told, §6.1 step 1); wear, restoration and abandonment (the world's slow course, receipted, never a docket item — they decide nothing between two parties); the DM's own verbs. **The three choices** (requirement 24): at a one-week advance the DM may leave the week to the engine, tilt it, or give the verdict; the hearing seal is read FIRST by ST's resolvers. **Only on the week:** each kind is minted only at the DM's one-week advance and lives that week; a month, season or year advance resolves every week on the default and leaves each week's receipt; nothing queues (requirement 24's binding on every kind). **The docket:** ST registers its FIVE resolvers with SP-9 (`registerEngagementKind`; `site_sale` added in round 4, L-BD 30); with `hearingWeekEnabled` dark the default resolves in its tick. **One contest per site per week** (A.18): whatever courts, patrols or bodies move on one site in one week meet it in ONE hearing with one draw — the anchor court leading, the rest joining — never two contests and never a second card for the same fact. **The card** (requirement 24(g), the Evidence Law): who, upon whom, where, the default — "Brigands under the Red Hand have come to the abandoned keep at Thornwatch. Left alone, they hold it." · "Kell's levy has marched on the robbers at the Crossed Keys. Left alone, the levy drives them out." · "The keep at Thornwatch, Kell's last, stands empty. Kell may send a garrison." · "Ashford asks the Grey Lady's flock to give up the watchtower above the town for grain. Left alone, the flock yields." (`site_sale`, L-BD 30) · "Kell and Tolle have ridden out together against the robbers at the ford." (one contest, A.18) On scrutiny the card names its READ (the force's band against the holder's might, in the might words; against a tied garrison, its readiness word — "Kell's keep at Thornwatch: manned" — never an army word, A.10). **RN:** a court's clearing mints no deed until RN's ENGINE-SOURCE slot opens; ST names its candidate source row `site_verdict` for that slot (RN §3.1).
### PR hunt
