83:- **THE BODIES (`DESIGN_FP_ARCH_BD.md`, compiled 2026-10-18) and its routes to PR (`cure/L-BD.md` §4; BD §19's PR row)** — a body (a gang, a conclave, a beast) is a traveller the ONE encounter law meets (§8.1), a foe of `patrol_engages` (§11.2), the quarry of THE HUNT (§5.5), and a watcher of the same law when two bodies meet (BD §9.1); BD's words bind here: "a patrol's coverage on an UNKNOWN trail is ZERO; on a known WATCHED trail it is the round's coverage at the junctions" (BD §5.2), "Patrols pursue only what their court marks `hunted` or `outlawed` (and every beast); a `permitted` conclave is NEVER pursued; `curbed` is watched, not hunted" (BD §7.1) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's routes (1)–(7)].
117:**PR5 — ONE DANGER, ONE COUNTERFORCE, AND NO GATE ROW.** Patrols change ONLY these quantities the world already keeps, each by ONE bounded lean at ONE named seam (§6, §7): (a) a SUBTRACTION on the ONE presence term of the danger ledger, inside the one suppressor slot of MN §3.3's composition — THE SHARED PRESENCE COMPOSER, a shared leaf-first car (RULINGS-ROUND3 A.3) — (ST's sites and PR's riders, one shared cap), floored at zero, never on the walls term — so a patrol lowers only what raiding menaces and untied dens ADDED to the country's roads — never the walls term and never an enemy column (MN §3.3) — and "peacetime roads carry no danger to relieve" (the host document) holds by construction; (b) a bounded DEVIATION term on the raider row's counterforce, and a coverage term on the criminal corridor's, riding ST's ONE additive post-blend slot under its ONE clamp — reaching a raiding menace's wear only through the stamped counterforce score (MN §5.5 (2)); (c) the banditry ROLL for goods on a watched hop (PR6); (d) the smuggling success chance at the worst gate (§6.4); (e) the field army's SEED at deploy, by the riders kept (`patrolDraw`, PR3) — never the per-tick `offensive` or `homeDefense`; (f) the commons' ONE grievance home, by ONE registered input (over-patrolling, §7.5); (g) the WITNESS read PS consumes (PR10); (h) PR's own WILL gate, by a magistrate's step (§10.5). The hearings and receipts of §9–§11 decide between parties and change nothing else. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-28: "three numbers … and no other" was false against §6–§7; the full list is stated and §7.2's second grievance input is struck · PR-r2-7: MN's slot (2) is filled through the stamp, never added · SEAMS-r2-7: the composition is MN §3.3's one sentence, cited and not restated.] PR NEVER mints a stressor birth gate row: the landed rows "Standing defenses patrol the approaches." and "A practised watch chokes smuggling at the gates." already ARE the standing watch, keyed on the institution roster; a second row would count the same riders twice. PR never touches the ramp's own security relief (`rampThreat`'s `W_SEC × security01`, the watch inside the walls).
125:**PR9 — REACT, GROUP, DISPERSE, BY BELIEF AND BY EFFECT.** A believed threat pulls riders toward it; a threat believed bigger than one patrol's band draws several into ONE detachment of the summed band; when the threat is gone, beaten, or was never there, the detachment disperses and its riders go back to their rounds. Grouping and dispersal are internal acts (receipts, no hearing). A FALSE REPORT therefore costs a town its watch for as long as it takes to look and find nothing — the effect of belief, priced by the world itself. Off their round the riders also HUNT (§5.5): a body their court has marked `hunted` or `outlawed`, or a beast, is pursued at the place the town BELIEVES it went — its last sighting, the trails the town knows, its habits — until it is caught or the trail goes cold; the round they leave goes unridden meanwhile, and a rider outmatched shadows and calls for others, never engages [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (3) · L-BD 20].
127:**PR10 — THE WITNESS IS THE PATROLS'.** `witnessedCrossing` (PS8) is owned here: a crossing is witnessed when a patrol of the HOLDER walks the holder's half of the gate's road that week (the placement, PR4) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-6 · SEAMS-r2-8: per power and per half; a power-blind MAX could not say "the holder's"], or, under a STRONG banner, a rider of the kingdom's net stands on the holder's half (§10.3 (d): the kingdom's eyes are one) [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — the owner's "operate in unity to cover the entirety of the kingdom region": a net rider placed on a member's half by right sees for that member; the GATE's catch stays the holder's own riders' (J385, §6.4)], or the crossing's PLACE is the holder's own seat (a harbour landing or a circle arrival — never a land crossing whose path merely runs on through the seat), or the unit is too large to hide, or a held watchtower stands on the stretch (ST17). On a HIDDEN WAY (THE BODIES' `trail:<a|b>`, PS8's quiet crossing taken off the road) the place is the TRAIL and ONE arm applies: witnessed only where the holder KNOWS and WATCHES the trail and its riders cover the trail's junction half that week (`trailWatchOf`, §2.6; BD §5.2: "a patrol's coverage on an UNKNOWN trail is ZERO") — the stretch-rider, seat, size and watchtower arms do not apply to a unit off the road (the trail's capacity is the hiding law, PS8). A town with no riders is blind to its roads; the quiet crossing succeeds only where no patrol walks [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — the PS→PR routes of `cure/D-PS-r4.md` §5 (applied in this round so none is left unapplied): the trail arm, and the seat arm re-worded (PS's REFINED 3: read literally on a node-keyed path, "the holder's own seat is on the path" would witness every intermediate land crossing, and P8 / R14 could never pass)].
163:`roundOf(worldState, snapshot, settlementId, tick) → [{ half: { road: [a, b], holder: seat }, priority, cadence }]` — the town's ROAD HALVES: its own half of `road{seat, n}` for every digest neighbour `n` whose territory meets the seat's; aspatially the relationship-graph edges at the seat (one half each). A round never leaves the town's land, so a round never crosses a border (only a pursuit or an escort beyond the gate does — §10.1(c)). ORDERED by a fixed-order priority score (DRAFT weights, UNMEASURED): THE ARMY'S ROAD while the town's army is on campaign — the halves of the deployment's path out of the seat through the town's own land, its supply road, first of all (§3.2) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-3: the brief's "an army on campaign needs patrols on its supply roads most" had no priority term] · believed danger on the half (the town's belief of dens, menaces, bands and hostile units on it — §5.1) · its trade value (the caravan traffic the road carries: `commodityFlow`'s channel strength across it, the entrepôt toll it pays) · recent incidents (the town's in-horizon `patrol_report` receipts and banditry losses on it — and, where HB is lit (`habitConditioningEnabled`), weighted by the town's LEARNED HABIT of riding that stretch: HB's ONE curve on the settlement actor, credited when a report finds a `clash`, a `catch` or a `threat_seen` there (`habit/habitCurve.js :: applyCredit`, "`const step = learnRateFor(lawWord) * severityWeightOf(outcomeRung);`"), read through `habitFactor` ("An ABSENT stock returns EXACTLY the number one") as ONE bounded multiplier on the incident term, under HB's LANDED circumstance class `route_menaced` with the stretch key as its action token — no thirteenth class (`habitVocabulary.js :: HABIT_CLASS_CEILING = 12`: "A thirteenth class is an owner gate, not an edit"), a town's single-digit halves inside `habitCurve.js :: HABIT_TUNING.HABIT_ROWS_PER_ACTOR_CAP` ("`HABIT_ROWS_PER_ACTOR_CAP: 24,`"); PLAUSIBLE until HB-0's car-0 admits a stretch-keyed token, and dark the incident term is the in-horizon count alone) [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 39's "the patrol's round biases toward incident stretches on the curve — PR's round, HB's weight": "a town raided from the hills learns to ride the hill road", with HB's one law and no second learner] · the trails the town KNOWS (THE BODIES §2.3: `spatialLedgers.hiddenWays.known[seat]`, BD's one writer `bodies/hiddenWays.js`, plus the warden office's ways while CH's warden archetype holds the town's public-security office, L-BD 41 — §5.5): a known trail `trail:<a|b>` runs beside the road `stretch:<a|b>` (BD §5.2: "its JUNCTION is that stretch"), so the town's own half of that road gains the KNOWN-TRAIL term — the choke point ("The BELIEVED junctions … are the patrols' choke points: PR's round plans by them") — and a known trail BD's record marks `watched` puts that half FIRST, as a fort's attachment does [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (4)] · a fort's attachment (ST §7.4's coverage row for PR — a held `fortification` at hand puts its halves FIRST on its holder's round; the riders who walk them are the holder's own, and the keep's GARRISON is the site's own complement whose road rows stand beside theirs, §10.5, RULINGS-ROUND3 A.1) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — A.1: the r2b "walls without riders are walls" denied the keep its own garrison's road rows] · the DM's order (§11.1). The round's ORDER is derived each week; the week's resulting placement is written once (§2.7 `placement`). [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — R-3: the brief's "beat" is the estate's NEWS BEAT (CHAIR-NOTES 2 "a bounded handful of beats"; WC §7.C "The beat inventory"); the patrol's route is its ROUND, the state `on_round`.]
187:When several riders act together (§5.2) they form ONE detachment: `{ detachmentId, settlementId, members: [ordinal…], allies?: [{ settlementId, members }], band, aim, place, sinceTick, causedBy, pursuedRef?, leaderRef? }` — `aim ∈ DETACHMENT_AIMS = clear · screen · pursue · escort · look` (`look` is a detachment of one). Its band is the members' summed latent strength, banded on the same five words. An allied town's riders — or a fellow member's under the banner (§10.3) — who JOIN (§10.2) keep their own command inside it (two commands on one stretch, WC's mirror-the-leg idiom) and are credited separately. `pursue` serves TWO quarries, never more: PT's road WATCH (a `party_ambush`, PR19 — its target is the card's, never stored here) and a BODY (THE HUNT, §5.5) — whose ref is `pursuedRef: { kind: 'body', id }` (the sixth actor kind, RULINGS-ROUND4 A.12) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (3): `pursue` widened from the party's watch to bodies]. `leaderRef: { kind: 'person', id: <wnpcId> }` names a HUNT'S LEADER where a mission is taken (L-BD 40, §5.5) — a REFERENCE only: PR never moves a person's record, and no verdict on the detachment ever touches the leader (no named fate) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 40: "the detachment under a named leader"]. Both fields are drop-when-absent additions declared under OD-PR-45 (the owner's shape, visible). Tokens: `pursuedRef` and `leaderRef` FREE in `src` and `tests` (`cure/D-PR-r4-probe/tokens-r4.out`; `leaderRef` has one prose hit in a ledger doc, another surface); `quarry` (34 src files, 8 quoted literals — the stone quarry) and `leader` (42 src files) AVOIDED as bare names.
197:- `believedWatch(worldState, snapshot, observerId, roadKey, tick) → { watch01, known }` — what a court BELIEVES the watch on a road to be, from NAMED producers (§8.3): its own riders' `riders_seen` reports at a shared gate, its allies' exchanged reports, its travellers' return receipts, its spies' product, rumor of a clash or a catch on the road; with nothing heard it returns the TIER-REFERENCE PRIOR of the road's holder (the coverage a funded town of that tier fields at peace) with `known: false`, and the card says "unknown" — the ONE planning read [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-16: no producer was named and `null` was undefined]. Its return is `{ watch01, known, phase? }` — `phase` the BELIEVED period and slot where two or more sightings on the half fix them (§2.3's learnable clock; L-BD 39); a TRAIL key `trail:<a|b>` is read too: `watch01` is the believed watch of the trail's junction half where the observer believes the holder KNOWS the trail (it has heard of a catch on it, or of a warden holding the holder's public-security office — §5.5), else 0 with `known: false` — never the holder's true knowledge; and for a BODY observer the read is BANNER-BLIND (the MAX over every power it has heard of on the road, whoever's riders they are — "A BODY sees one banner", RULINGS-ROUND3 F.4) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (7) · L-BD 39 · L-BD 41 (b)].
198:- `trailWatchOf(worldState, snapshot, power, trailKey, tick) → watch01` — THE ONE COVERAGE READ ON A HIDDEN WAY (BD §5.2): `knownAndWatched(power, trailKey) ? watchOf({ road: 'stretch:' + pair, holder: power }, tick, power) : 0` — the power's riders on its OWN half of the junction road (a trail runs through the power's land only where it runs beside a road the power holds a half of; under a strong banner a net rider standing on that half by right counts for it, §10.3 (d)), and ZERO on a trail the power does not know or does not watch (its known set: BD §2.3's learned ways with their `watched` mark — BD's field, BD's writer — ∪ the warden office's ways, which are known AND watched by the office's trade, L-BD 41; BD §5.2: "on a known WATCHED trail it is the round's coverage at the junctions") [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (4): "a patrol's coverage on an UNKNOWN trail is ZERO"].
199:- `predictedPlaceOf(worldState, snapshot, settlementId, bodyId, tick) → { place, confidence, reasons } | null` — THE HUNT'S PREDICTION (§5.5), on BELIEF only: the town's newest sighting of the body (BD's `believedBodies`), the trails the town knows, and the body's habits (BD's `BODY_HABITS`); `null` when the town has nothing to go on. One read for every mover that follows the hunt (the detachment; a paragon leader's own mover, CH) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (3) · L-BD 20 · L-BD 40].
200:- `bannerCoverOf(worldState, memberId, fromTick, toTick) → { placed, weeks, powers }` — THE BANNER's ONE read of PR's own (§10.3 (f)): the riders of any power other than the member's own that stood on its road halves in a span, from the placement digest's `lived` rows — the fact PL's protection row reads. The LOYALTY STACK is PL's BANNER STACK (PL §2: `polityOf(…, homeId).path` with `crownReachAt` at each rung, CUT at the first `swornLinkSuspended` link — "NO NEW READ"), and whether a crossing is BY RIGHT is PS's `passageStandingOf(…).banner` (`right · tolerance`; PS §5.5) — PR keeps no read of either [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.7, aligned with PL §2/§4.7 and PS §5.5].
