213:**Persisted shapes: ONE new (four maps of one ledger)** — with THREE drop-when-absent fields added in round 4 (`forkSince` on `placement`; `pursuedRef` and `leaderRef` on `detachments`), each DECLARED AS THE OWNER'S SHAPE and visible for his veto (OD-PR-44 · OD-PR-45; their lifecycles §16.1) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — PR-W1 · BD's route (3) · L-BD 40]. **Rows added to landed shapes (no new shape):** ONE conditional stamp on the landed deployment record — `patrolDraw: { riders, points }`, written by ONE conditional line in the opener beside the seed only when the points ACTUALLY drawn are above zero (`if (drawn.points > 0) seededRecord.patrolDraw = { riders: drawn.kept, points: drawn.points };` — the landed idiom of the line after it, "`if (coalitionDecision) seededRecord.joinLedger = [coalitionDecision.anchor];`"; `seedDeploymentState`, `warArmyRecord.js` 72 eff, is not edited) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — PR-W2 · PR-W3: the line is counted (PR16, §14 PR-1), and `points` is the strength actually drawn, never more than the offensive it came from] (the W-C1 receipts' "stamp ONLY when non-trivial" idiom; absent ⇒ the record is byte-identical), read by the stage to bound the riders fielded while that army is out (§3.2) and by the siege's Why line [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-1], validated fail-closed by its own block in the deployment normalizer (§16.1) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — PR-V7]; the `patrol_report` feed entries with their typed content (`{ kind: 'patrol_report', finding, roadKey? (a stretch key), power?, band?, subjectRef? }`, `finding ∈ threat_seen · crossing_seen · riders_seen · found_nothing · catch · clash`; the rumor ledgers' own lifecycle) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-16]; PS's crossing rows written with `witnessed` from PR's read (PS's shape); ONE `MOVEMENT_SITES` row (a test manifest); the registry rows of §11.2 (SP-9's ledger); the realm-manifest row of `PATROL_ORDER`.
246:3. **Detachments advance** (§5): converging riders arrive (their leg priced by `namedPersonLegTicks`), engaged detachments resolve their hearing's verdict or default (§11.2), a hunt moves to this week's predicted place (§5.5), finished errands DISPERSE (a receipt) — a hunt also when its trail goes cold — and detachments past the rest bound send their riders `resting` (§7.3).
247:4. **New detachments form** from believed threats (§5.2), hunts (§5.5: a pursued body believed in the land; a mission taken under a named leader), looks (§9.2), escorts (§10.4) and the DM's order — each drawing riders from the round in reverse priority (the least important stretch loses its rider first).
263:- a DEN — a site attached to the town held by an UNTIED holder (ST §2.1: a body — a gang or a beast, THE BODIES' ref `{ kind: 'body', … }` — a menace, or a villain; never a conclave, whose site is a church's, RULINGS-ROUND4 A.3) that the court knows of: not under the court veil (`keptSecret`, ST §2.4 — the map's `hidden` word was withdrawn there), for a kept-secret den is learned only by WITNESS — a look's finding (§9.2 (b)) or the warden's ways (§5.5) — and makes no `den_unanswered` (RULINGS-ROUND4 A.16) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.3 (the struck `band`/`cult` holder kinds) · A.16 (the veil's word and its witness)];
264:- a BODY — THE BODIES' gang, conclave or beast the town has heard of (BD's `believedBodies(worldState, observerId)` → `{ bodyId, bodyKind, lastWhereId, lastWhat, lastTick }`, from the town's rumor records carrying the body's id, truth in the omniscient arm), its band the believed might; a THREAT the riders ride against only where the court's stance toward it is `hunted` (a gang) or `outlawed` (a conclave), or it is a beast (§5.5; BD §7.1) — a body the court lets be is no threat to ride at; WC-12's located brigand body IS BD's gang record (BD's route to WC) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's route (6): the slot "WC-12's located unit (UNBUILT: a slot; until it lands the ambient raider stressor has no body to ride to)" is filled];
