284:A detachment DISPERSES — its riders return to `on_round` the next week, a `patrol_dispersed` receipt with `causedBy` the finishing verdict or report — when its contest resolves, when the threat is no longer believed (the town's belief has moved: a later report, the rumor's TTL, the threat gone — a hunt's COLD TRAIL is one, §5.5), when the DM's order ends it, or at the rest bound (§7.3).
286:### 5.5 THE HUNT — riders after a body (the owner's ~19:0x word: "patrols when not in routine patrolling are trying to predict and catch up to gangs, beasts, and hostile conclaves"; THE BODIES §9.3, which cites this section; L-BD items 20 · 39 · 40 · 41) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's routes (3) and (5) · L-BD 20 · 39 · 40 · 41: "the hunt is PR's text; BD cites"]
288:- **THE PREDICTION, ON BELIEF.** A pursued body the town believes in or beside its land (§5.1) is ridden for at its PREDICTED place, `predictedPlaceOf(worldState, snapshot, settlementId, bodyId, tick)` (§2.6), from three things the town holds and nothing it does not: (i) its newest sighting — where and what (`believedBodies`' `lastWhereId`, `lastWhat`, `lastTick`); (ii) the trails it KNOWS (BD §2.3's learned set ∪ the warden office's ways, below) — an unknown trail is never predicted; (iii) the body's HABITS, BD's closed `BODY_HABITS` read (its leaf `bodies/bodyHabits.js`, BD-5; BD §9.3: "a gang returns to its den, a pack follows the season, a flock goes where the faith is fractured") — THIS body's own habits where HB carries the body grain (L-BD 39 (c): "the patrol's PREDICTION … reads THIS body's habits (not the kind's)"), else its kind's. Never the body's true position (K3); `null` (nothing to go on) ⇒ no hunt, and the town waits for word.
289:- **THE PURSUIT.** A detachment with aim `pursue` and `pursuedRef: { kind: 'body', id }` (§2.5) forms by §5.2's rule — one rider whose band reaches the body's believed might, else the fewest riders whose summed latent points reach it, drawn from the round in reverse priority — and each week rides to the predicted place on the light-unit physics (`namedPersonLegTicks`; one place a week, PR1). The CATCH is the ONE encounter law on TRUTH (§8.1's body arm): MET only if the body is really there and the riders stand on that road half, that known trail's junction, that site or that country; NOTICED by the law's draw against the body's cover. Met and noticed ⇒ `patrol_engages` (§11.2), the house's band contest with BD's `bodyStrength`. A catch on a trail TEACHES the town the trail (`by_catch`, BD §2.3's writer).
290:- **THE COLD TRAIL.** When the town's newest sighting is older than `COLD_TRAIL_WEEKS` (DRAFT 3, UNMEASURED) — `tick − lastTick`, read from `believedBodies`, so nothing is stored for the dwell — the trail is COLD: the detachment DISPERSES (§5.4) and the round resumes. A sighting by a shadowing rider, a report, a raid heard of — any fresh word — keeps it warm.
292:- **SHADOW AND GROUP (the second).** A rider OUTMATCHED by the body's believed might never engages: it SHADOWS — follows the prediction and reports (`patrol_report` `threat_seen`, §9.3), keeping the trail warm — while the town groups (§5.2) or asks an ally (`patrol_joins`, §10.1 (d)); under a strong banner a fellow member's riders may ride to it by right, still that member's decision on a `patrol_joins` card (the banner spares the crossing, never the choice — §10.3 (d)).
293:- **OVER-PURSUIT (the third).** A hunt is bounded by the rest bound (§7.3) and the cold trail; beyond the town's border it is PS's ladder (an ally welcomes hot pursuit as urgency, §10.1 (c)) or the banner's right (§10.3 (d)); a hunt that rides into a body stronger than it believed is `cut_down` (§7.2) — the price of a wrong belief.
